WEBVTT

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:21.680
Seriously! There's no end!

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.190
Flicker, burn them so the surrounding
houses aren't affected!

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:27.480
It's impossible in such
a closely built location!

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.530
So many of them!
Where did they come from?

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:34.780
They're golem-like zombies
made of soil and vegetation.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.410
We can destroy them,
but they come right back.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.580
We need a more fundamental solution...

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.580
That carriage is...

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.540
Garrett!

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.300
Garrett! Wake up, you!

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:59.430
"Episode 5
'I Am Reborn!'"
Use the armored jeep's flamethrower to
take out the zombies in one fell swoop...

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:02.560
What are you saying?
Get a hold of yourself!

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.350
An angel?

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:10.980
Which means... is this heaven?

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:13.820
It's me, you idiot!

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.280
Zombies usually only appear at night,

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.990
but today, it was just past noon when
they began roaming about town.

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.620
After a while, beast-shaped zombies

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.000
also appeared and began
to attack the residents.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.710
And what actions did you take?

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:29.420
Yes. The Warriors' Union is the shelter

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.050
and the Mages' Union is the infirmary.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.130
Right now, the zombies are being handled

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:38.800
by Knight Patrol, adventurers, and
residents who know how to use weapons.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.390
I see.

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:45.180
I myself am on duty at the request
of the union, so please excuse me.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.390
Mm.

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:54.360
Is that soldier someone you know, Mira?

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:55.990
First time we've met.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.240
Tact, you should stay
with Emella for a while.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.160
What about you, Miss Mira?

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.300
A moonlit funeral procession
with no prayers,

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.010
a grave marked by a sword with no body.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.680
The hands that guide are the brilliantly
colored emissaries of heaven

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.140
that wheel down from the sky.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:26.180
Maidens of war, who lead
to carnage the departed souls

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:29.020
that have left the eternal cycle of life.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:32.110
The reverberating clash of
weapons sound a requiem

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.770
and build a span of rainbow
unto the heavens.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.780
Crossing the night sky, descend!

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:41.700
O choosers who don prismatic colors!

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:02.010
We seven sisters have come
in answer to your summons.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.100
Mm, I appreciate that.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:08.350
I saw Alfina earlier, but I have not
seen the rest of you in a long time.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:10.060
Have you been well?

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:13.860
Yes! Except for dear sister
Alfina’s training sessions!

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:14.900
Oh!

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.070
Shh, she'll hear you!

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:23.620
It's too late. She heard me.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.740
I am sorry you had to hear
that silly business.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:30.210
I will reprimand Christina later,
so please forgive us.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.620
You are the same as ever.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:36.380
So, is your training really that grueling?

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.510
No, it's no such thing.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:42.340
It's easy training that emphasizes
repetition of the basics.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.970
Hm, is that so?

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.220
That was easy? She's kidding, right?

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.480
Then, what would difficult
training be like?

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.560
But!

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:57.020
It's not easy to swing
a sword 100,000 times, is it?

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.150
Well said!

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:00.820
On this occasion, I agree with Christina.

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:05.070
One hundred thousand times, you say?
That sounds a tad high.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:07.580
No! We're still lacking in skill!

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:12.660
In order to be of help to you, Master,
we must train more and more!

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:19.420
Alfina, perhaps you should
provide for some rest as well?

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:21.920
I don't know when I'll
call you in the future.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:23.970
If you are tired from training,

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:27.390
I will not be able to count
on you whenever I need you.

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:31.930
This is...

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:34.440
I will review what we do in training!

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.900
Master, my deepest apologies.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:41.570
Well, as you can see,
I'm thinking of leaving the job

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:46.490
of cleaning up the zombies in this town
to you, but can you do that?

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.740
Yes, but my sisters are tired--

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:50.580
Please leave it to us!

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:55.170
Such spirit of devotion to offer
themselves up for our master!

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:57.880
I, of all people...

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:01.710
I will also help so that I will not
be outdone by my sisters!

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.300
Yeah!

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:07.340
It feels like their morale
is improving in a weird way...

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.800
We are hereby appointed to this mission!

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:14.100
We seven sisters go
at the will of our master!

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:23.440
I am here to help!

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:47.090
Master, an urgent matter.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:49.760
Please look up at the sky.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.430
What's that?

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:55.020
Based on the nature of its magic,
we believe it is a half-demon.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:56.230
A half-demon...

00:05:56.230 --> 00:06:00.230
A so-called abomination born between
a demon and a human...

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:02.400
It appears to be dead.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:05.190
So, zombies both in
the sky and on the ground?

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:08.910
The source is unknown,
but we believe these zombies

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:14.120
were created by the unnatural mana
blanketing this whole region.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.750
Hm, and that is the mana?

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:20.880
Yes. It can be applied in various
ways depending on how it's used,

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.250
but what shall we do with it?

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:25.260
There's no need. Quash it.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.760
Understood.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:31.760
Speaking of which, I've defeated
a half-demon before.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.810
Is that so?

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:38.060
Since I was still unskilled at the time,
I struggled a lot,

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:40.270
but if it's him, it'll be troublesome.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:45.280
Then now is the time. Let's destroy him
before he is completely revived.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:47.990
He is not fully revived yet?

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:51.030
No. Please leave it to us sisters.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:53.200
Mm, very well.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:59.040
On my honor. To get this done,
I have a request of you, Master.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:01.250
Your permission to use a new technique.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.500
Huh?

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:09.090
My sisters!

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:15.100
Now is the time to
bring together our power!

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:47.340
Shoot to kill!

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:07.570
Oh-ho! So that was "Imitation Code G"!

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:19.200
The half-demon and the magic
in the surrounding area

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:21.290
have been completely annihilated.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:26.040
Mm. Everyone, thanks for your hard work!
It was a splendid technique.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:28.800
We're honored by your praise.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:31.670
Now, make sure to get some good rest.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:35.840
Yay!

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:44.690
That guy moved!

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.070
Mother...

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:58.240
Good job!

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:07.000
Thank goodness! Thank goodness
everyone is safe and sound.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:08.880
You are being dramatic.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:12.090
Emella was giving it
everything she had, after all.

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:15.340
Without the kind of power you have,
Mira, worrying the way Emella did

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:17.180
is about the right amount of worry.

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:18.800
R-Right.

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:21.430
Anyways, evocation magic is amazing.

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:23.980
Ah! You can appreciate it?

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:27.770
I mean, if you can summon, you can call
the beautiful Valkyrie ladies all you want

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:30.730
and make all the harems you want.

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:33.360
That is not what evocation magic is for!

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:38.490
But I also want to use magic and
become strong like Miss Mira,

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:41.280
and help everyone someday.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.040
Tact...

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:46.710
Tact, why not check if you have
the aptitude to become a mage

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:47.870
at the Mages' Union?

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:49.790
Aptitude to become a mage?

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:53.250
It's late today, so you
can go see them tomorrow.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:54.090
Okay!

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:57.760
Perfect timing. I'll be departing
tomorrow, but before I do,

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:02.470
I can see the birth of a future summoner.
That would not be half bad.

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:05.640
What?! Mira, you're leaving?!

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:07.690
You can be my child!

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:10.650
What do you mean, "my child"?

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.570
You guys are lively.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:13.900
Captain!

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:18.950
Good evening. I am the captain
of Écarlate Carillon, Cyril.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:23.620
It seems our members are indebted
to you, so thank you very much.

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:26.040
It's nothing you need to thank me for.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:29.120
It was a lot more fun than going alone.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:30.210
Mira!

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:32.090
Hey! Don't get too close!

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:35.170
--Has Flicker been causing
you trouble by any chance?
--Seriously, you are so adorable, Mira!

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:37.880
--A great deal, in the same vein as this.
--Seriously, you are so adorable, Mira!

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.760
--I apologize for that.
--Seriously, you are so adorable, Mira!

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:41.470
Well, I do not mind.

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:44.850
Now, is it time to distribute the loot?

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:49.100
I say that, but Mira beat almost all
the monsters by herself today,

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:51.600
so I don't know that we should be
splitting things equally.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:53.270
That's a lot.

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:56.230
Oh, even Mobility Crystals. How rare.

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:59.200
Mira says we should divide these up, too!

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:01.160
Talk about her generosity
knowing no bounds.

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:04.450
I think we can distribute
the demon materials as well.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.660
But is it really okay if we take these?

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:12.460
You're so tedious. I like you guys.

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:15.960
Put it this way.
Just think of it as your reward

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:19.300
for all the good that you
have fostered in the past.

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:22.550
Now, then, that just leaves
this giant scythe.

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:24.510
How heavy is this?!

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:28.020
This is what those dark knights
are swinging around?

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.730
Indeed...

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:34.400
Man, I drank a lot!

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:38.320
By the way, Mira,
you're leaving tomorrow, right?

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:40.200
Please let me see you off.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:42.160
There's no need to do that.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:45.160
No, there's also something
I'd like to talk to you about,

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:48.120
so please let me treat you
to lunch if I may.

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:49.660
At this place.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:50.830
Understood.

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:53.080
Well then, until tomorrow.

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:58.210
That man. Could he be...?

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:05.100
Thank you! You're so kind!

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:06.390
What is this?

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:08.640
I have been waiting for you, Mira.

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:09.560
Oh.

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:14.350
He wants to be a summoner,
so can you check his aptitude?

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:16.110
I would appreciate it very much!

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:18.860
Yes, let's find out right away.

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:23.450
I will be counting on you. I've been
called in by the union leader.

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:33.500
Dates? Also, Solomon's showy signature.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:37.210
May 12, 2146.

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:40.710
The document I had to fill in when
registering as an adventurer

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:45.140
said May 19th, but it's been a
week since I came to this world.

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:47.680
This D is basically "Danblf"...

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:53.730
The other letters are likely Flonne,
Luminaria, Kagura, Artesia...

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:57.860
He said he checked
the Friends List every day,

00:12:57.860 --> 00:12:59.690
so I suppose those who aren't written here

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:03.820
were here in this world before Solomon.

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:06.280
Still, Solomon, that sly bastard.

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:08.240
Seriously, the way
he presents this sort

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:10.790
of additional information
is so like him...

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:12.580
Miss Mira.

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:15.370
Tact, did you get the test results?

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:18.380
This is Tact's aptitude to become a mage.

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:22.380
He has the aptitude to become
a sorcerer, priest, or diviner.

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:24.130
I also measured his capacity for magic--

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:26.800
it was far above the average.

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:28.970
Tact has a promising future.

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:31.260
So, not to be a summoner.

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:34.600
Will I be able to become like you now?

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:39.060
Yes, work hard, and I am sure
you will become a fine mage.

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:42.030
When you do, let us go on
an adventure together.

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:43.320
Yeah!

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:49.620
I am sure we will meet again someday.

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:56.750
Oh, right! This was an option!

00:13:56.750 --> 00:14:02.000
With this, there will no longer be
a need for me to wear frilly clothes!

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:05.090
Hm, where shall we begin?

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:07.720
I'm sure you don't have much time,

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:11.430
so I'm fine with getting straight
to the point with meta talk.

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:15.430
So, as I suspected,
you are a former player.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:16.480
Yes.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:21.360
So, we were using the "Inspect"
function on each other yesterday?

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:25.190
If you find someone amazing,
the first thing a player always does

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.610
is do a status check with "Inspect."

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:29.660
That's true...

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:33.580
So, Mira, how long have
you been in this world?

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:35.410
Just a week.

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:38.830
You look quite calm considering.

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:40.170
Around that time,

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:44.380
I was desperately looking for a way
to return to our original world.

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:48.300
If I didn't have my friend,
I'm sure I would have been as well.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:50.760
It's thanks to my friend.

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:54.140
You're Danblf, right?

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:55.270
Yes.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:01.100
Though, now, I'm being
run ragged by that person.

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:05.690
Even so, you were fortunate
to find your friend quickly.

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:08.820
I went through a lot
and it took me a year.

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:11.990
That long? The place I
woke up happened to be

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:15.200
a place where my friend was likely to be.

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:17.250
I was lucky.

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:21.540
Oh, that reminds me,
I hear you're Danblf's pupil?

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.920
I had never heard that
the Wise Men took pupils.

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:27.590
Could it be that he's
your real-life friend?

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:30.380
Who is this person?!
His intuition is uncanny!

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:32.890
The story of yesterday's adventures
that I heard from Emella

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:35.810
sounded somewhat similar to
anecdotes about Danblf, so...

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:39.890
Oh, maybe you're actually Danblf himself.

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:42.060
Y-Y-Y-You are correct!

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:43.730
He is my real-life friend.

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:48.440
Both he and I always played
independently in the game!

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:51.030
Did I fool him? Did I fool him?

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:53.660
I see, so that's it.

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:55.830
I fooled him!

00:15:57.410 --> 00:16:02.120
Never mind about me.
Won't you tell me about yourself?

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:07.750
I came ten days after the First Day.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:10.670
The First Day?

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:13.590
I will never forget. It was a rainy day.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:15.890
In a place where I had
no idea where I was,

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:20.180
I saved a widow with a baby from goblins.

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:21.560
Watch out!

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:25.400
Wh-What?

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:28.530
It hurts! It hurts!

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:30.570
And for a while now...

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:32.070
What is this?

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:34.160
The smell of grass on a rainy day...

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:36.490
The feeling of hair clinging to me...

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:40.620
And... dripping from my palm...

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:43.000
...the warmth of my blood...

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:48.800
U-Umm... thank you for helping--

00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:50.880
Why didn't you run away?

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:56.640
There, there.

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:59.970
I never heard that they
implemented babies...

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:02.980
An NPC? No way!

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:08.440
Hanna's husband apparently died
from a rainy goblin's poison dart.

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:13.320
Not only that, but because of them, it had
become difficult to harvest the crops,

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:17.410
so she has had a hard time
raising a child by herself.

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:20.540
What is this?

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:24.910
What happened? I can't even logout...

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:29.790
And everyone on my Friends List
is displayed as offline.

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:32.710
All I see there is a mother and child.

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:36.680
They don't seem like NPCs
being run by the system.

00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:41.560
I went to a shop in town to heal my wound,
but there was no medicine,

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:45.810
and I found out a trader would be
coming from the Kingdom of Alcait.

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:49.480
Alcait! Solomon's kingdom!

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:52.280
If Solomon is alive and well as a king,

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:55.990
I might be able to go ask him
about this strange situation...

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:59.030
There wasn't anyone
who could prepare medicine.

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:02.410
But if we were able
to converse in this way,

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:07.710
I speculated that the NPCs
just might be able to learn.

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:10.500
Won't you please sell me
your herbs, Hanna?

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:14.800
Oh, no! I couldn't take money
from someone who saved me!

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:20.930
No, this is for your future,
and more specifically, for the village.

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:25.980
I passed on what I already
knew of medicine to Hanna,

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:28.600
while I also deepened my own knowledge.

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:32.650
Then, I eradicated the rainy goblins

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:37.530
and taught the villagers
the minimum means of self-defense.

00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:39.570
Furthermore, I also touched
on the topic of business

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:43.120
and passed on everything
I knew of negotiation skills.

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:46.580
I hoped that this village
could become independent.

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:47.710
Then...

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:52.000
Thank you very much!

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:54.550
It should have been a hard-luck story,
but somehow or other,

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:57.590
I couldn't help but feel
like it had been fun.

00:18:57.590 --> 00:18:59.380
Even though this is a time of crisis...

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:04.010
You, too? To think we would now experience

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:06.140
that sense of excitement
of just starting the game.

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:10.770
After that, I reunited with my friends at
the Adventurers' Guild Union in a big city

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:12.310
and was helped by various people.

00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:17.570
I found more friends and people
who identified with me,

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:20.700
and that's how I launched my guild.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:26.160
However, what we can accomplish
is limited by our reach.

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:30.210
There were numerous times when
things were beyond my grasp,

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:31.830
even though I desperately
tried to reach out.

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:34.380
To know this world and to help
the people in this world...

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:38.260
Mira, won't you join my guild?

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:45.390
I'm sorry. I may not look it,
but I am quite busy, you see.

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:48.270
I'm not able to put myself in a group.

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:51.690
Of course. I figured I had
nothing to lose by asking.

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:54.270
And I had a hunch that
there would be no way.

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:59.360
However, if I hear a call for help,
I'll do my best to respond.

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:00.780
How about that?

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:05.490
Yes, thank you very much.
I'd like to show my gratitude, but...

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:10.750
Could I have you look into this?

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:14.000
I knew it, Mira!

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:17.630
You did know the soldier
in that runaway carriage!

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:20.880
--I'm going, too!

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:22.590
--You!
--I'm going, too!

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:29.640
I got a lot of souvenirs.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:34.270
A meat burger from Asval.
Bean tea from Zef...

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:37.860
These suit me.

00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:42.570
A thank you letter from Tact. How cute.

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:47.990
A letter from Flicker. Wow, it's thick...

00:20:47.990 --> 00:20:50.750
A novel from Emella...

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:55.920
"<i>Danblf Romancing Adventure</i>
<i>Mysterious Saga</i>"?

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:59.000
Wait, this is a novelization of me.

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:03.760
We've been waiting for you.

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:05.050
Mm.

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:09.140
This way please.

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:13.350
What do you say?

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:15.560
I am reborn!

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:19.650
I also cleared the quest!

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:22.690
No, it looks good on you. Really...

00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:25.490
I've come back!

00:21:25.490 --> 00:21:27.120
Welcome back.

00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:29.490
Miss Mira, your appearance...

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:33.120
This? It looks fine, does it not?

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:35.830
And what of you? What is that?

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:37.460
Well...

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:42.090
When you left without a word,

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:45.130
it seems it came as quite
a shock for Mariana and...

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:47.760
I have been helping out.

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:50.140
I-I see...

00:21:51.680 --> 00:21:54.560
Miss Mira! Welcome back!

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:55.770
That robe!

00:21:55.770 --> 00:21:57.730
What do you think? Fine, is it not?

00:21:57.730 --> 00:21:58.610
Yes!

00:21:58.610 --> 00:22:02.980
It's a replica of Master Danblf's robe,
which is very popular with the children.

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:04.400
Huh?

00:22:04.400 --> 00:22:07.990
Children? A replica?

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:19.460
So, that's why!
